translations.text:
Do not say its treasure is spent,
that it lacks subjects and the lyre has fallen silent;
there may be no poets, but there will always
be poetry.

While waves of light at the kiss
throb, all aflame;
while the sun clothes the ragged clouds
in fire and gold;

while the air in its embrace carries
fragrance and harmony;
while spring still exists in the world,
there will be poetry!

While science has not yet reached
the sources of life,
and in sea or sky there is an abyss
that defies calculation;

while humanity, ever advancing,
does not know where it is going;
while there remains a mystery for humankind,
there will be poetry!

While we feel the soul grow glad,
though our lips do not smile;
while we weep, though tears do not come
to cloud the eye;

while heart and mind
continue their struggle;
while hopes and memories remain,
there will be poetry!

While there are eyes that reflect
the eyes that gaze into them;
while a sighing lip answers
the lip that sighs;

while two souls can feel themselves
mingled in a kiss;
while a beautiful woman exists,
there will be poetry!

Lofty mountain, where Rome’s devastation
will forever proclaim your memory;
proud buildings where the glory
of great Carthage still shines;

deserted shore, once a peaceful lake,
filled with triumphs and victories;
shattered marbles, a history
that shows us what the world repays;

arches, amphitheaters, baths, temple,
celebrated buildings that you were,
whose traces we now scarcely see;

your example is a great remedy for my pain:
if time brought you down,
time can bring down my sorrows.
